{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeRmHcv9y81VVi8n9py3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate `personal_markov_coin_belief`, and the self-check printed `OK`.\n\n**The idea:** each person has their own belief about how often a fair coin switches between H and T from one flip to the next. They judge each sequence by how likely it would be under that belief. They then pick between the two sequences in proportion to those likelihoods. This works out to the chance of choosing the left sequence being sigmoid(difference in number of switches × that person's believed switch log-odds).\n\nThe person-level belief has a population distribution (mean `mu`, spread `sigma`, non-centred, 400 slots), so the next design can still predict new participants. The model is aimed at the critique's strongest finding, which survived the FDR correction: people differ in their preference for alternation far more than the current best model allows (observed SD 0.16 vs 0.05). Existing models describe one shared population and no person-specific coin belief, so this mechanism is new to the set.\n\n**Self-check:** this was a short smoke fit (100 draws, one chain), so it doesn't tell us whether the model will converge or how it will rank. Its ELPD-LOO came out at −1253.2. The best model in the set, `local_representativeness`, sits at −1380.4, but that is from a full fit, so the two numbers aren't directly comparable. Two warnings came up:\n- **Convergence not checked:** a single chain can't report R-hat. Admission's full fit will apply the real convergence gate.\n- **PSIS-LOO unreliable:** 2.1% of trials have a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance. That's likely because each person has their own parameter. If the full fit shows the same, the model's ELPD-LOO will be marked as untrustworthy.\n\nNot checked: whether it is different enough from the existing models to pass the novelty gate.\n\nFiles are in `.../experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2192,"cache_read_input_tokens":48286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2192,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":652,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34d079f4-9195-40c6-910a-f23215a39973","uuid":"c0fe738f-375a-4bed-b400-bdc247fcacab","timestamp":"2026-10-03T01:22:16.367Z","request_id":"req_011CfeRmHF653ZBGGXMjf1E6"}
